# edi-run DECISIONS.log — newest at TOP

## 2026-11-19 — LOC counting ruling: `probes/loc.py` code-line count is the official measure (Owner: S2)

**Ruling (Owner: S2, 2026-11-19, "I agree. Proceed").** The official line count for the 1,777 cap is the **code-line count produced by `probes/loc.py`** (non-blank, non-comment lines across the five core files: `edi.py`, `gates.py`, `loop.py`, `adapters.py`, `metering.py`), enforced in CI by `probes/loc.py --check`. The **weighted** count (e.g. 120-character weighting, used by external reviewers) is **informational only** — it is reported in reviews but never gates a release. This matches Decision 2 of the 2026-11-18 round (Option A — Code-Line Cap `1,777`, `MAX_PHYSICAL` retired): blank lines, `# G:<id>` markers and readable wrapping are not penalized.

**At v0.1.2 (tag, 2026-11-19):** 1,718 code lines / 1,998 physical lines (1,718 ≤ 1,777).

## 2026-11-19 — Ruling A: Authorship and Seats (`Briefing_for_the_edi_run_maintainer_0_1_0_operator_skill_defects.md`, PR #17)

**Ruling (Owner: S2, 2026-11-19).** Confirmed the recommended path: **keep the runtime rule** — the Operator never authors the bar, rubric, method or seed; and the author of bar/rubric/method never sits as Maker or Evaluator (the seed's author never sits as an Evaluator). Defects 1–2 of the 2026-11-19 briefing fixed as written; the alternative (operator authors its own instruments) was rejected — it would drop a separation `gate_authorship` already enforces.

**Implemented (PR #17, commits `f3533be` + `57c32d1`, merged to `main`):**
- `gates.py gate_authorship`: refuses at freeze when an AUTHORSHIP.md bar/rubric/method author equals `maker.name` or any `evaluators[].name` (canon compare), or the seed author sits as Maker/Evaluator — preflight and real freeze now agree.
- `SKILL.md` §4/P1 rewritten: the operator scaffolds and transcribes verbatim; "you author all content" removed.
- `docs/2026-EDI-OPERATOR-SKILL-SPEC.md` §2 carries both rules and names `gate_authorship` as the freeze-time enforcement point.
- Same PR also fixed briefing defects 3–6, all minor items, and the 2026-11-18f release review `A1`–`A8` (scaffold CR-2 fields, clean run-refusal, per-operator watch marker, `--seed-dir` copies, secret-scrub span redaction, `repo_root` EDI_REPO refusal, README CI section + the fork-PR-on-self-hosted-runner risk flag).

**Gates at merge:** external repro `repro_skill_0_1_0.py` **6/6** (0/6 red before); ADDITIONS-6 **8/8** (1/8 red before); suite **281 OK**; LOC **1,652 ≤ 1,777** at merge (1,665 after the Ruling A gate additions — `probes/loc.py` is the authoritative count); probe gate 14 PASS / 0 FAIL / 1 KNOWN-FAIL / 5 SKIP (baseline); CI all green on both PR heads.

**Scope correction (Owner, 2026-11-19, same day).** The first implementation of the seed-author clause refused a seed author seated as **Maker** too — that overreached the ruling (which bars the seed's author only from Evaluator seats) and blocked the raise-bounds successor path `loop.py` offers (re-freeze a successor carrying the incumbent forward: the incumbent's author IS the producing Maker). Fixed in `f052a37`: the seed-author refusal now checks Evaluator seats only; successor case added to `tests/test_operator_skill.py` (positive freeze + negative seed-author-as-Evaluator). Repro `repro_successor_0_1_1.py` passes.

**Posture decisions carried in `cb6c1de` (0.1.1 feedback batch):** the `~/.hermes/.env` key fallback is OPT-IN (`EDI_KEY_FALLBACK=1`) — Owner posture, shared-host leak class; freeze now fails fast when a direct model seat's key resolves empty (non-loopback endpoints; agent seats exempt — their relay fails fast at run time), naming the remedy. `common.repo_root()`'s `~/Code/edi-run` fallback REMOVED (hard refusal: `EDI_REPO` or in-repo only) — installed skill copies must declare `EDI_REPO`. Both marked **Breaking** in `CHANGELOG.md` (new file; also documents the v0.1.1 `record_summary` score-shape change). The successor repro is committed as `probes/repro_successor_0_1_1.py`.

**Still open (tracked):** key→host binding in `adapters.py`; CL1-15 self-vouching `readBy` in `loop.py`; the undelivered guarantee map; Maker/Evaluator seat-bot disposition (adoption plan D3). (The LOC counting ruling is CLOSED — see the 2026-11-19 LOC ruling at the top of this log: `probes/loc.py` code-line count is authoritative; the weighted count is informational.)


## 2026-11-18 — Five Readings-Mode Fixes (`edi-run-memo-readings-fixes-2026-11-18.pdf` & `NOTE-TO-MAINTAINER-2026-11-18e.md`)

**Source.** Owner memo `edi-run-memo-readings-fixes-2026-11-18.pdf` (Fixes 1–5) and Grok Bot `NOTE-TO-MAINTAINER-2026-11-18e.md` (`RD2`, `RD4`, `RD5`, `F1`/`N21`).

**Fixes Implemented (`1,643` code lines across the 5 core files, `<= 1,777` enforced by `probes/loc.py --check`):**
- **Fix 1 / `RD4` (`loop.py:verify_job`)**: In `mode: "readings"`, `verify_job` reports custody integrity rather than requiring `disposition == "given"` and `outcome == "census"`. A `needs_owner` or `no_observation` readings job closed by the Owner with `--disposition declined` or `--disposition given` now exits `0` from both `finalize` and `verify`.
- **Fix 2 (`loop.py:read_job`, `edi.py`)**: `edi.py read <job_dir>` freezes (if needed) and runs the job, prints the terminal state and the exact `edi.py finalize` command for the Owner, and never writes a `disposition` event on its own (`--by` dropped from `read`, keeping disposition strictly a human Owner act).
- **Fix 3 / `RD5` (`loop.py:verify_job`)**: In `mode: "readings"`, `verify_job` re-hashes every `check` event's `evidence/reading-*.json` file against its recorded `evidence.sha256` and every file in `artifact/` against the last `artifact-produced` event, failing if any file is edited or deleted after `finalize`.
- **Grok `RD2` (`loop.py:_parse_reading`, `_eval_batch`)**: Requires a reading's whitespace-normalized `quotation` to appear in the judged text (the candidate artifact or control case); ungrounded quotations mark the evaluator failed (`needs_owner / no_observation`).
- **Fix 4 & `N21` (`tests/test_trim_requirements.py`)**: Updated `test_n15` to treat Linux zombie processes (`state == 'Z'` in `/proc/<pid>/stat` when PID 1 does not reap orphans) as dead, and strengthened `test_f1` to test a kill in Round 2 with an existing Round 1 incumbent followed by `finalize --disposition declined`.
- **Fix 5 / `Q3` (`README.md`, `docs/2026-EDI-Runtime-Solution-Architecture.md`)**: Documented that `vendor/record.py verify job.jsonl --files` runs from inside `<job_dir>` for modern job-relative logs (while the three pre-P5 examples run from repo root), and added `examples/live-aider-job11` verification from its folder to `README.md`.
- **Traceability correction to the earlier 2026-11-18 entry below**: In `edi-run-memo-line-cap-readings-2026-11-18.pdf`, Decision 7 was where a readings job keeps its limits (`bounds`), whereas the `edi.py read` convenience verb originated from the earlier R1 ruling (`docs/DECISIONS.log`). Corrected below.

## 2026-11-18 — Owner Ruling: 1,777 Code-Line Cap, Readings Mode (`census`), & Post-18d Hardening

**Ruling (Owner: S2, 2026-11-18).**
> *"Owner ruling: the 1,500 line cap was arbitrary target. Let’s raise it to 1,777 lines so we can make corrections and add back the 'readings' mode."*
Followed by **"Proceed"** approving Option A across Decisions 2 and 4–8 (synthesizing Grok Bot `18d`, OpenRouter Claude Opus 5.5, OpenRouter GPT 6.2 Sol, and `edi-run-memo-line-cap-readings-2026-11-18.pdf`).

**Decisions & Changes Executed (`1,637` code lines across the 5 core files, `<= 1,777` enforced by `probes/loc.py --check`):**
- **Decision 2 (Option A — Code-Line Cap `1,777`, `MAX_PHYSICAL` Retired)**: `probes/loc.py` enforces `MAX_CODE = 1777` and drops `MAX_PHYSICAL` so blank lines, `# G:<id>` comments, and readable line wrapping are never penalized.
- **Readings Mode (`mode: "readings"` / `census`, `C29`, `D4.6`, `D5.outcome.census`)**:
  - `gates.py`: Validates `mode in ("scored", "readings")`; in `readings` mode requires `bounds.max_rounds == 1` (or absent; Decision 7 of `edi-run-memo-line-cap-readings-2026-11-18.pdf`: limits stay in `bounds`), requires Buyer approval on `bar.digest`, refuses Specialist approval (`C29`), and refuses `scale`, `threshold`, or `floor` on dimensions.
  - `loop.py` & `adapters.py`: Supports both Entry B (`seed` draft) and Entry A (one Maker turn); prompts model Evaluators for `{"outcome": "conforms"|"does_not_conform"|"unobserved", "quotation": "<non-empty quote>"}`; validates reading slots (`_parse_reading`: numeric score, unknown word, or blank quotation marks the evaluator failed -> `needs_owner/no_observation`). All dimensions `conforms` across all runs (`R >= 2`) -> `accepted/census`; any run-to-run disagreement records all outcome words in `disagreements[]` (`D4.6`) -> `needs_owner/no_observation`; any `does_not_conform` reading or all-`unobserved` dimension -> `needs_owner/needs_owner` with `escalation.json` (never `rejected`).
  - **Decision 4 (Option A — `custody/v1` Boundary for Readings Mode)**: Because vendored `vendor/check.py` (`CL1-3`) hard-requires a Specialist approval and has no `census` field, `finalize_job` in `readings` mode appends the `disposition` event to `job.jsonl` (carrying `mode`, `terminalState`, `outcome`, `disagreements`, `acknowledgesUnobserved`) without calling `make_record.py` to emit a falsely-failing `record.json`, and `verify_job` verifies `job.jsonl` (`custody_verify` including all file digests), `job-pin`, and the `disposition` event.
  - **`edi.py read <job_dir>` (per R1 ruling; updated by Fix 2 above)**: Convenience verb for `mode: "readings"`.
- **Post-18d & Verification Audit Fixes (`F1`–`F7`, `N14`, `G-CUS3`, Cuts 0c & 2)**:
  - **`N14`**: `loop.init_job` creates only `("scripts", "seed")`, never `rounds/`.
  - **`F1`**: `Meter.recover()` returns the count of recovered reservations and `loop._open_meter` re-anchors `state.json` when recovery adds rows, so `finalize --disposition declined` after a `SIGKILL` mid-call succeeds cleanly.
  - **`F2`**: `adapters._run_seat` sets `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` and `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX`, `gates.tree_manifest` pins any `.pyc` outside `__pycache__`, and `gates.gate_commands` refuses seat commands referencing `RUNTIME_WRITTEN` or `NEVER_AUTHORED`.
  - **`F3`**: `adapters.run_maker` sets `meter._round = round_no`, and `loop._resume_job_held` filters already-amended call digests so double-resume on the same round never double-amends prior calls.
  - **`F4`**: `Meter.hold()` settles at worst-case reservation cost if an exception occurs after upstream dispatch, and `_UnixProxy` joins its request threads on shutdown.
  - **`F5` & `F6`**: `loop.freeze_job` holds `job_lock(job_dir)` when `not dry_run` and anchors `demo_meter` in `state.json`.
  - **`F7`**: Resumed rounds scope batch IDs and evidence filenames by attempt (`B1-a2`, `reading-*-r1-a2-run*.json`, `harness-*-B1-a2.json`).
  - **`G-CUS3`**: Restored `examples/live-aider-job11/job.json` to match its `job-pin` sha256 and added a `job-pin` check to `loop.verify_job`.
  - **`N9` (Documented Window)**: Confirmed `WINDOW = 32 / MIN_LINE = 16` is pinned by `test_briefing.py` (`FindingC_FilterPrecision`: a 21-char common phrase must not be scrubbed) and documented the exact threshold (`>= 32`-char sliding windows and `16..31`-char whole lines) in `docs/2026-EDI-Runtime-Solution-Architecture.md` and `README.md`.

## 2026-11-18 — Minimalism QAR Refactoring & Trim (Opus 5.5 + Grok Bot Review Bundle)

**Ruling (Owner: S2, "Proceed" on Decisions 1–7, Option A across all 7).**
Core LOC across the 5 runtime modules (`edi.py`, `gates.py`, `loop.py`, `adapters.py`, `metering.py`) had grown to **3,016 physical lines (2,191 code lines)** at `d3a3721`. Following the Opus 5.5 + Grok Bot review bundle (`~/Desktop/Edi-run/20261118-244-review/`), all 7 verified runtime defects were fixed and the structural cuts were executed to bring the core down to **1,737 physical lines (1,496 code lines, 43 `# G:<id>` comment/doc lines, 198 blank lines)** — enforced in CI by `probes/loc.py --check` (`<= 1,500` code / `<= 2,000` physical).

**Defects Fixed:**
- **R1 / N13 (`loop.py:freeze_job`)**: Deleted the pre-gate `job.json` write so a refused freeze leaves `job.json` byte-identical on disk while keeping the post-gate atomic `job.json.tmp-freeze` write before `job-start`.
- **Q1 / N12 (`metering.py:output_bound`, `loop.py:freeze_job`)**: Required a positive finite `max_output_tokens` at `freeze` (`bounds.max_output_tokens` or `pricing[<model>].max_output_tokens`) for every model/agent seat so unbounded output is refused at `freeze`, never mid-run.
- **N8 (`loop.py:run_job`, `resume_job`)**: Wrapped `run_job` and `resume_job` in `with job_lock(job_dir):` (`_run_job_held` / `_resume_job_held`) so concurrent `run`/`resume`/`finalize` invocations serialize cleanly on the job lifecycle lock (verified 5/5 by `N8x5`).
- **R3 & Q2 (`gates.py:tree_manifest`)**: Replaced the 3 separate seat-file walks and 65-line AST Python import walker with a single `tree_manifest(job_dir)` that pins `{rel_path: sha256}` of every file under `job_dir` except `RUNTIME_WRITTEN` and `NEVER_AUTHORED` (`__pycache__`, `.DS_Store`, `*.pyc`). Fixes `finalize` failing when Python writes `__pycache__/*.pyc` during `run` (**R3**) and pins `held_out/` inside `pins["tree"]` (**Q2**).
- **R4 / N2b (`loop.py:run_job`, `resume_job`)**: Resumed rounds never move or overwrite `rounds/round-NN`; new attempts write to `rounds/round-NN-a2` (recording `"dir"` in `state["rounds"][r]`), so every path in `job.jsonl` stays immutable on disk and unmodified `vendor/record.py verify --files` passes on resumed jobs.
- **N11 (`metering.py:Meter.hold`, `adapters.py:_chat_json`)**: Wired direct model Maker and model Evaluator calls through `with meter.hold(...)` so every paid seat call gets a durable pre-call reservation and provider-side `max_tokens`/`max_completion_tokens` injection.

**Structural Cuts Executed:**
- **Cut A1 (`adapters.py`)**: Deduplicated 12 HTTP response blocks in `_Proxy.do_POST` into `_Proxy._reply()` and `_Proxy._refuse()`.
- **Cuts C + B′ (`metering.py`, `loop.py`, `adapters.py`)**: Merged `usage.resv.jsonl` into `usage.jsonl` as a single hash-chained spend ledger carrying `reserve`, `call`, `release`, and `amendment` rows (3-element `anchor()`), dropped `anomaly` rows from `usage.jsonl` (Decision 6A), called `meter.recover()` on `Meter` construction inside `run`/`resume`/`finalize`, and removed `adapters._admission_closed`. Retired 15 dual-ledger mechanism tests and added `tests/test_trim_requirements.py` (11 requirement-level tests).
- **Decision 4A (`adapters.py:sandbox_prefix`)**: Dropped `/opt` and `/var/lib` from the `bwrap` read allowlist, binding only `/usr`, `/bin`, `/sbin`, `/lib`, `/lib64`, `/etc` plus the resolved `sys.executable` prefix.
- **Cut F & Grok Cuts 2–9, 14**: Unified seat subprocess execution onto `adapters._run_seat()`, extracted `_fence_prompt()`, removed `loop._accrue`/`_cost_of` (deriving `token_usage` from `meter.token_usage()`), and replaced multi-line review-history comments in the 5 core modules with single-line `# G:<id>` invariant tags.
- **Cut G (`examples/`)**: Replaced the 9 declined scaffold directories (`examples/live-aider-job`..`job10`) with a 10-job defect-ladder summary table in `examples/live-aider-job11/README.md`, scrubbed host paths and `*.lock` files, and added `*.lock` to `.gitignore`.

## 2026-11-18 — Round-3 deep-review defects: disposition and implementation notes

**Disposition.** All nine deep-review defects (P1–P9), the operator-skill items,
and the NOTE-to-maintainer's four priority items plus its medium items that the
round-3 ask named were implemented and gated RED-first on
`tests/test_briefing_r3.py` (15 tests, delivered unchanged as the acceptance
gate) plus new concern-named tests (`test_proxy_spend.py`, `test_probe_gate.py`,
and additions to `test_briefing.py` / `test_operator_skill.py`).

**Decisions taken in implementation (Owner-visible, not new doctrine):**
- P1 job pin: `gate_instruments` adds a `job` pin (canonical sha256 of job.json
  minus its `disposition` block); a new `gates.check_pins` names which pin moved
  and run/resume/finalize compare through it. Nothing else moved.
- P2: amendments are labels, not subtractions — `accrued()` counts every billed
  call; `discarded()` reports the labelled subset (design doc R1 section
  amended in the same change; the four tests the briefing listed as updated
  were updated, none weakened beyond that).
- P6: `finalize` refuses a mid-round or best-artifact-no-end-state job unless
  the disposition is `declined`; `run`/`resume` refuse once a disposition
  exists in the chain.
- Exit codes: the briefing's 0–6 table implemented in `edi.py` only; `loop.*`
  still returns 0/1/2 for library callers. SKILL.md, `record_summary.py` (5 =
  FAILED) and `cost_report.py` (spend from usage.jsonl, cap from job.json)
  updated to match.
- P7: `freeze --dry-run` makes no paid CL3 demonstration calls and says so on
  stderr; a real CL3 freeze meters the demonstrations and a cap trip there is
  a `GateError`.
- NOTE items: the proxy RESERVES each call's worst-case spend under the meter
  lock before forwarding (parallel calls cannot race past the cap — disclosed
  residual: reservation is the conservative estimate, actual usage above it is
  the same one-call overshoot already disclosed) and refuses `stream: true`
  (400, refused calls logged to `proxy-usage.jsonl`). Seat-command files in any
  language anywhere in the job are pinned (`seat_files` pin). The escalation
  watcher dedups per-job by (mtime_ns, size) instead of one `-newer` marker, so
  new escalations are never missed even when their mtime ties the marker.
- Probes/CI: the probe gate's S1 entry is macOS-only (Linux skips it — the
  allowlist already passes it there; the KNOWN_FAILS entry names the seatbelt
  posture); CI requires a WORKING sandbox on both legs (sandbox_usable probe
  step) and fails the leg instead of letting agent tests skip silently.

**Not done (out of scope per the briefing):** self-signed CL1-15 evidence;
controls the judge can tell apart from real work; injection canaries in the
live examples' planted controls (optional); readings mode (R1) still awaits a
ruling. The live examples' $0 pricing is now documented as non-re-runnable as
committed (README) — supplying real rates remains an Owner call.

## 2026-11-18 — Review bar demoted from standing gate to tiered (Owner: S2)

**Ruling.** The hardening sprint is over; the last three changes were flip-a-default
scale, and carrying a deep + adversarial frontier review pair as a standing gate on
every change was drifting toward the Plumbline failure mode (ceremony growing faster
than evidence). Tiered bar, effective now:

- **Deep + adversarial frontier reviews** — required only for changes touching
  `adapters.py` or gate semantics (gates.py, loop.py freeze/finalize paths).
- **Everything else** — full suite + probe gate + CI green. Those already catch the
  invariant regressions; reviews add no marginal signal at this change size.
- Review-artifact tests are re-homed by CONCERN (tests/test_sandbox.py,
  tests/test_briefing.py), never stacked as dated strata per review round.

